"[HEADER] Installation Infos",
"kill",
"When you click 'START SETUP' in the 'SETUP' tab, psychonauts.apworld will be installed and moved into the 'custom_worlds' folder inside the Archipelago Launcher directory. Astralathe Mod Launcher inside the game's directory. The required AP Mod folder 'PsychoRando' will be installed inside Psychonauts\\ModResource. The selected 'RandoSeed.lua' file will be placed inside the 'PsychoRando' folder.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] apworld / yaml Infos",
"kill",
"Psychonauts is not a core Archipelago game, it needs a custom world file. When 'psychonauts.apworld' is downloaded in the Archipelago Folder (by clicking START SETUP), boot-up the Archipelago Launcher and go to 'Options Creator' to create your .yaml file and then, when you're done, send it to the person who will host the AP Multiworld.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Connection Infos",
"kill",
"Once the setup is done, the host of your Archipelago session will need to go to the Archipelago website and go to the room that you are going to use for your Archipelago session. There, you should be able to find a button that says 'Download Patch File' next to your name. Download it, and once you have it, you can move on to the next step.\n\nExtract the patch file folder (should be something similar to 'P1_quack!_Gx4hEFheQIy4hE3bQTv89g.zip')\n\nIn the 'Server' field, enter archipelago.gg.\n\nIn 'Port' enter the room’s 5-digit port number. You can find this number on the website after creating a new room.\n\nIn 'Slot', enter the name assigned to your YAML file.\n\nThe 'Password' field is optional. If the host did not set one, leave it blank.\n\nFinally, click 'Connect' and then, you can start a new run!\n\nNow, go back to the game and you should be able to start a game while connected to the AP server! :)",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Revert Infos",
"kill",
"You have 2 revert options, both can't be enabled at the same time.\n\nIf you use the 'Clear AP Mods' option it will only delete the mods that are required for Psychonauts Archipelago.\n\nIf you use the 'Full Clear Astralathe' option it will delete everything related to Astralathe Mod Manager and mods. If other mods are detected an additional confirmation will appear.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] PopTracker Infos",
"kill",
"Some games have a PopTracker integration for Archipelago which allows you to track all possible Locations, Items, Upgrades, Zones, Hints and more depending on the game.\n\nFor the setup there are 3 different cases:\n\n\t• If the selected directory does not contain a PopTracker folder (or any similarly named folder), a new 'poptracker' folder will be created and the pack will be downloaded to poptracker\\packs.\n\n\t• If the selected directory already contains a folder with 'PopTracker' in its name, the installer will look for a poptracker.exe file. If one is found, the pack will be downloaded to its packs folder. If no poptracker.exe is found, the folder will be renamed to 'poptracker' and any missing files or folders will be created.\n\n\t• If the selected directory is already a PopTracker folder (for example: C:\\Users\\magni\\Documents\\poptracker), its contents will be validated. If everything is present, the pack will simply be downloaded to poptracker\\packs. Otherwise, the folder will be repaired before the pack is installed.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Troubleshoot",
"kill",
"If you launch the Mod Launcher for the first time with the launch option related to it and it says that some framework or mods are required, it shouldn't do anything and I would assume it is just a false error (seems like it).\n\nIf you game doesn't launch with the AP Mod loaded when using the Client, open the Mod Launcher and make sure the 'Archipelago' mod is enabled.\n\nFeel free to report anything (or simply join the discord) here!",
